Z||000015||RoadRocket||09-10-2001||09:16 PM||||I have seven different answering machine messages, all of which were rotated everyday (when my computer was working), each with a different theme:<BR>Star Trek, Mission Impossible, Rocky & Bullwinkle, Clint Eastwood, Star Wars, The Who, and James Bond.<P>The Clint Eastwood one goes, for example, like this: <BR>&lt;VOICE="Clint Eastwood"&gt;<BR>I know what you're thinking. Did the phone ring two times, or was it three? Is Ed Dana at home, or is he away? Well, there's one thing you have to ask yourself. Do you feel lucky? Well, do ya?<BR>&lt;/VOICE&gt;<P><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Cheever3000||09-10-2001||09:32 PM||||I once recorded a greeting on ours, in a Henry Fonda voice: "Chuck & Robin aren't here right now.  They're out swimmin' in Golden Pond.  I don't think they'd be swimmin' in it if they knew what made it golden.  But leave your name & number and they'll call you back."<P>I've done em using a Rocky voice and Jimmy Stewart also.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Patrick's Dad||09-11-2001||09:08 AM||||My best was similar to one of the above,<P>"Hi, it's me. I'm screening my calls right now, so leave a message. If you're someone that i want to talk to, I'll pick up. If not, leave a message, and I'll call you back if I feel like it."<P>The background music was provided by the encore from a live recording of my friends' band, Clinic. When Dan (the lead singer) heard it, he would leave messages imitating himself leading into the encore....||||reg||1
